@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+# Trailer audio
+
+The mix is built from the `audio` list in `edl.json`; clip audio is always dropped by the renderer.
+
+## Game audio
+Unity Recorder's movie output doesn't record audio reliably, so either:
+- record game audio separately (Recorder's Audio recorder, or route the output through a loopback device) and add
+  it as an `audio` entry starting at the clip's position in the trailer, or
+- rebuild it: export the SFX the shot plays (`Assets/Audio/SFX/...`) and place them in the mix at the right times.
+
+## Music (ElevenLabs `music`)
+Pass a `composition_plan` so the music's sections line up with the beat sheet, one section per beat group:
+```json
+{"positive_global_styles": ["orchestral hybrid", "pulsing synth bass", "120 bpm"],
+ "negative_global_styles": ["vocals"],
+ "sections": [
+   {"section_name": "Cold open", "positive_local_styles": ["sparse", "tension"], "negative_local_styles": [],
+    "duration_ms": 6000, "lines": []},
+   {"section_name": "Build", "positive_local_styles": ["drums enter", "rising"], "negative_local_styles": [],
+    "duration_ms": 20000, "lines": []},
+   {"section_name": "Climax", "positive_local_styles": ["full", "big hits"], "negative_local_styles": [],
+    "duration_ms": 18000, "lines": []},
+   {"section_name": "Title", "positive_local_styles": ["final hit", "ring out"], "negative_local_styles": [],
+    "duration_ms": 6000, "lines": []}]}
+```
+Each section is 3-120 s, the whole plan at most 10 minutes. The tool returns the item id and path; cut the edit
+list on the section boundaries (sum of `duration_ms`). Music needs a paid ElevenLabs plan.
+
+## Voice-over and SFX
+- `tts` for VO lines (one file per line, so lines can move independently); `list_voices` to pick a voice.
+- `sound_effect` for whooshes, hits and risers (0.5-30 s).
+
+## Bookkeeping
+Copy every file you use to `T/audio/` and record it in `T/audio/sources.json` (file, item_id, tool, credits,
+prompt or plan). For a licensed track record the source, license and attribution text in REPORT.md as well.
+
+## Levels
+Music around -14 LUFS integrated for the final mix; VO 3-6 dB above the music (lower music `volume` under VO
+entries rather than raising VO). Check: `ffmpeg -i out.mp4 -af ebur128 -f null -`.
