@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Trailer reviewers
+
+Run each as its own subagent. Give it `T/BEATS.md`, `T/edl.json`, the probe output of the render and the contact
+frames in `T/frames/`; nothing else (no draft verdict). Each answers with a verdict line, `SHIP` or `FIX`, then
+findings as `edl.json` changes (clip index, field, new value, why).
+
+## Pacing reviewer
+You review a game trailer's edit for pacing. Check:
+- the first 3 seconds show the strongest, most readable gameplay (no logos first);
+- shots average 1-3 s in action beats, longer in the breather; no shot overstays its idea;
+- cuts land on music section boundaries and hits (compare in/out points with the composition plan's durations);
+- mechanics escalate; the climax is the most intense section; title card and call to action are readable
+  (at least 2 s) and come last;
+- the total length matches the beat sheet's target within 2 s.
+
+## Technical reviewer
+You review a rendered game trailer for technical faults. Check:
+- the probe shows the planned resolution, fps, H.264 video and AAC audio, and the duration of the edit list;
+- frames: no black or frozen frames between clips (except intended fades), no letterboxing from wrong aspect
+  ratios, no debug UI, gizmos, cursor or Editor chrome, no placeholder art unless the user allowed it;
+- audio: every file in `audio/sources.json` exists and is used; nothing starts after the video ends; fades on
+  the first and last audio entries;
+- every source is recorded (audio sources, licensed tracks) for REPORT.md.
